inds of cards: medicine library card (form+strength) and medication/dose card (route + count + strength). The Plan/Home cards are dose cards, so route-prefixed is appropriate. The Medicines list shows the medicine definition, so form+strength. So perhaps not a bug?! Hmm.\n\nBut the changed item: \"Secondary caption on medication cards: its text is now resolved by a helper shared with reminders and the widget.\" This suggests medication cards (presumably on Plan/Home) now show the helper output: \"Oral · 3 mg\". And the Medicines list card is a different \"medicine card\" showing \"Tablet · 3 mg\" maybe intentional.\n\nUgh. Our reported bug was confirmed & logged by developer, so it is considered a bug (developer confirmed). Good. But maybe the actual expected is the opposite: The Medicines card should show \"Oral · 3 mg\" too. Whatever; confirmed. Moving on.\n\nLet's see the widget sample: \"Cyproterone acetate / Oral · 1/4 tablet · 12.5 mg\". Format includes \"Oral · 1/4 tablet · 12.5 mg\". For our Estradiol count 1, count omitted (\"Oral · 3 mg\"). For Testosterone count 2: \"Oral · 2 capsules · 100 mg\". This matches.\n\nNow reminder notification might show same. We could try to trigger a notification by creating a group whose dose is due soon. Hmm.\n\nLet's examine adding a new group with start time \"Now\" and daily schedule. In Add group screen, start time default \"Now\". If we create group at 7:20, dose scheduled 7:30 AM—actually times of day default 7:30, not start. Wait group schedule times of day = 7:30 AM. The start time is when schedule begins. So if current time is before 7:30, reminder at 7:30. Current time 7:20. We have ~10 min. Not feasible to wait 10 minutes? We could. But session budget...\n\nAlternatively set times of day to current+1 minute by editing group's 7:30 AM time picker. We can set dose time to 7:22. Then reminder should fire. But notification permission? App may not have notification permission granted. Check Settings \"Dose reminders\" on; notification permission may or may not be granted. If not, no reminder.\n\nCould be worth trying: edit group, tap 7:30 AM time chip, pick 7:22 AM, save, wait until 7:22 and check notification shade. But time picker interaction is complex. And current time may now be 7:20.\n\nActually maybe the reminders are not necessary to test; the area list is \"medication groups and cards, Settings, adding and editing medicines\". Reminders are mentioned only in changed item context. The sweep should focus areas. The widget/reminder are secondary.\n\nLet's instead thoroughly test medication group creation edge cases and medicine editing:\n- Group with no name? Save disabled? Test blank name.\n- Group with no medications? Can't save.\n- Duplicate group name allowed?\n- Group color change.\n- Weekly schedule with no days selected? Test.\n- Times of day: add multiple times, remove.\n- Start date/time picker.\n- Editing medicine name/strength validation (empty, 0, huge).\n- Removing medicine from group.\n- Archiving medicine.\n\nGiven time, prioritize potential clear bugs.\n\nLet's go back to the app. Press app from recents? open_app."}
