{"type": "thinking", "text": "No swipe action. Group archive may not be accessible from Plan (maybe archived groups only). Skip.\n\nNow, let's look for other potential bugs in the areas we haven't covered:\n\n1. Settings \"App lock\" toggle: enabling may require device auth, potentially lock the app. Skip (risky).\n2. \"Hide screen content\" toggle: affects screenshots/recents. Could test toggle and revert, but screenshot tool may fail. Skip.\n3. \"Dose reminders\" toggle: off/on persistence. Quick test? It's simple.\n4. \"Reminders may be delayed\" info row. Not necessary.\n5. \"App language\" English: changing language would be complex.\n6. \"Pure black dark theme\", Adaptive color, blur, classic nav: appearance toggles. Could test quickly but risk.\n7. \"Backup to file\" etc. Not necessary.\n\nMaybe the most likely remaining bug is in the changed Preparation form picker shared catalogue: perhaps certain categories should offer additional forms; e.g., \"Custom\" is missing Injection/Gel/Patch, or maybe \"Estradiol\" is missing \"Capsule\". Let's investigate by comparing app semantics. The shared catalogue probably defines forms:\n- tablet, capsule, injection, gel, patch.\nCategory-specific availability:\n- Estradiol: Tablet, Injection, Gel, Patch (no Capsule)\n- Antiandrogen: Tablet, Capsule\n- SERM: Tablet only\n- GnRHa: Injection only\n- Custom: Tablet, Capsule only\n\nIf it's a shared catalogue, maybe the catalogue maps forms to categories. Custom likely should allow all forms because it's custom. But if the catalogue is shared, it might intentionally constrain custom to oral forms? Hmm.\n\nMaybe there are other forms like \"Cream\", \"Spray\", \"Suppository\" missing? Can't know.\n\nCould test that switching category resets form to a valid option and no stale selection bug. E.g., Estradiol > Injection, then switch to Antiandrogen: does form become Tablet (valid)? We did earlier: tapping Antiandrogen changed to Tablet. Good. Switch SERM: Tablet. GnRHa: Injection. Custom: Tablet. No stale invalid states.\n\nWhat about selecting a category then switching form and back; do fields update correctly (strength labels)? We saw labels change correctly (Tablet strength, Vial strength, Gel concentration, Patch total amount, etc.). Good.\n\nOne potential issue: Estradiol > Injection > Vial > strength; then save; does medicine list caption show correctly? Could test but likely fine.\n\nMaybe duplicate medicine name allowed; but that's not clearly a bug.\n\nAnother idea: The \"Medication\" choices for Estradiol were only \"Estradiol valerate\" and \"Estradiol\". For injection, choices expanded to 5 (valerate, cypionate, enanthate, benzoate, undecylate). For tablet, only valerate and \"Estradiol\". Maybe tablet should also include estradiol hemihydrate etc. But unclear.\n\nTest \"Estradiol\" as medication (not valerate) with Tablet: display name auto \"Estradiol\", caption \"Tablet · x mg\". Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug in the preparation form picker: switching from Injection to Tablet retains \"Vial strength\" value or the wrong strength unit? Earlier when we switched Estradiol Injection -> Custom, the strength field label became \"Tablet strength\" fresh. Let me test switching forms back and forth with an entered value: select Injection, enter strength 5 mg, switch to Gel: does the gel concentration field retain the old 5? If the same underlying field is reused, it might incorrectly carry over the value across forms (e.g., \"5\" in Gel concentration %). That could cause a bug: stale data between forms. Let's test.\n\nGo Medicines > Add medicine > Estradiol > Injection, enter strength 5, then tap Gel: see if concentration field contains \"5\" (wrong) or empty. This is a good test of the shared catalogue/form switching. Let's do.\n\nMedicines > Add medicine."}
